   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT in relation to authorizing VFW Post 4927 to file an application for\nexemption from real property taxes for certain assessment rolls",
    "basePrintNo": "S8494",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S8494-2021",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "",
    "lawSection": "Real Property Taxation",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S8494\n\nSPONSOR: MATTERA\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act in relation to authorizing VFW Post 4927 to file an application\nfor exemption from real property taxes for certain assessment rolls\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nAllows VFW Post 4927 to file an application for exemption from real\nproperty taxes with the Town of Brookhaven in relation to the sale of\nreal property.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1. Authorizes that the assessor for the Town of Brookhaven may\naccept an application for exemption from property taxes owed on the\nproperty located at 34 Lamport Avenue. Upon granting such exemption, the\napplicable governing tax department shall have discretion to exempt\noutstanding taxes owed.\n\nSection 2. Enacting clause.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nVFW Post 4927 is a not-for-profit tax-exempt organization that missed\nthe tax-exempt filling status when moving locations. They have requested\nretroactive relief from property tax that would not apply to a non-pro-\nfit.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew Bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nTo be determined.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
